unless you've been living under a rock  odds are you've at least heard about  Bitcoin with prices skyrocketing in  recent months numbers like $20,000 have  piqued the interest of even the least  tech-savvy individuals you've probably  had an older relative ask you what the  heck is going on with the magic internet  money in this video we're not going to  get bogged down with all the technical  details there are plenty of other  excellent videos for that already some  of which you can find linked in the  description  instead use this video as a kind of  jumping-off point a place to start your  adventures in the world of crypto and  consider whether it's something you  should be invested in let's start with  the biggest question for most people  what is it to answer that we'll start  with a little history back in 2008 an  anonymous figure going by the name  Satoshi Nakamoto announced the release  of his invention a decentralized  peer-to-peer digital cash system this  was the beginning of Bitcoin Satoshi had  seen numerous centralized digital  currency projects fail and by opting for  a peer-to-peer system he managed to  create the very first cryptocurrency  instead of relying on banks to keep  transactions honest and prevent double  spending crypto currencies like Bitcoin  rely on what's called the blockchain on  the blockchain everyone sending and  receiving money has access to a public  ledger basically a list of global  transactions in order to make sure  future transactions aren't an attempt to  spend money that isn't there it sounds  weird and techy but it's actually pretty  simple imagine you're at a party and  you're betting on a game no one brought  cash so you all decide to keep track of  bets on your own individual sheets of  paper after each round everyone compares  their records with so many copies of  transactions any discrepancies would be  obvious and everyone is kept honest  for example if Steve says I only bet 5  bucks that round everyone else could  check their records and either verify or  challenge that claim that's the  blockchain in a nutshell this system  circumvents the need for a central bank  allowing truly peer-to-peer transactions  and minimal transaction fees ok but  what's a Bitcoin or litecoin or ether  and why are there so many different  currencies  here's the technical definition a  cryptocurrency is a digital medium of  exchange created and stored  electronically in the blockchain using  encryption techniques to control the  creation of monetary units and verify  the transfer of fun  it has no intrinsic value no physical  form and its supply is not determined by  a central bank think of the actual coins  like your online bank account  you see credit and debit transactions  and your current balance you can take a  debit card to the store and buy  something you don't need to have  physical cash the bank verifies you have  the money to spend and you get your  product bitcoin is the same way except  instead of a bank approving the  transaction it's the blockchain and just  like you measure foreign currencies  against your country's currency other  coins are usually measured against  Bitcoin and you can exchange them for  one another just like traditional  currencies as for why there are so many  different Kryptos or coins typically  each one represents a new technology and  development and when you buy some amount  of any given crypto you're supporting  that technology for example when you buy  Tron coins you're supporting that team's  goal of creating a block chain based  free content entertainment system that  enables users to publish and store data  when you buy electro neum you support  the goal of making cryptocurrency more  accessible to the average smartphone  user and the people who don't want to  get in over their heads with mining and  all the technical stuff each coin serves  a purpose and many people choose to  invest in the technology that they'd  like to see become mainstream of course  many other people just see the dollar  signs and that's ok too  there are plenty of stories of early  adopters buying Bitcoin when it was dirt  cheap and are now multi millionaires the  cryptocurrency market is booming and  people are flooding in trying to find  the next coin to explode an interesting  aspect of the crypto boom is that  investors are mostly young rather than  the older demographic which typically  has more disposable income to risk  trends indicate that this is well on its  way to changing with many expecting a  surge of new investors from all walks of  life within the next year so the big  question should you invest in  cryptocurrency well that's a question  you'll have to answer yourself but here  are some tips number one don't make any  investments thinking you'll be a  millionaire in a year you could be if  you invest enough and wisely but you  could also lose it all the crypto market  is incredibly volatile often compared to  the stock market on fast-forward as  currency values experience huge swings  on daily or weekly timeframes number two  never invest more than you can afford to  lose if 10 bucks and a promising coin is  all you can afford just invest the 10  dollars you  you can buy tiny fractions of coins you  don't need to spend tens of thousands in  order to get in on Bitcoin number three  do your research don't just go in  blindly find the white paper for each  coin you like and read it understand  what you're investing in you'd be amazed  how many people just throw money into  coins without knowing what they're for  okay so you decide to jump in what are  the first steps you'll need a count on a  few sites coin base is a good place to  start though it does have relatively  high transaction fees it's a very easy  way to buy a few of the biggest coins  namely Bitcoin and aetherium but wait  what if I don't want Bitcoin don't worry  you can exchange your Bitcoin for  whatever coins you like next you'll want  to bookmark coin market cap to keep  track of coin prices and only buy when  the price is right the next step is to  make an account on an exchange like  finance cracking or crypto PIA not all  coins are available on all exchanges so  you may want to set up an account on  several on these sites you can set your  exchange pair for example Bitcoin to XRP  but before you buy your coins you'll  want to download a wallet for whatever  currency you choose there are various  mobile apps to store some currencies but  many smaller coins require a specific  wallet for the time being to stick with  the ripple example you can download rip  X wallet and set up your account follow  the instructions very carefully you  don't want your information to get lost  and lose access to your coins once  you've got your wallet set up you can  exchange your Bitcoin and deposit your  new coins into your wallet there are  slight differences between how you buy  different coins and ways to dodge  transaction fees but there are plenty of  excellent tutorials on those subjects  which I'll provide in the description  along with links to all the sites  mentioned over the course of this video  the world of cryptocurrency is  fascinating and exciting and there will  be lots of world-changing new  technologies and plenty of new  millionaires made in the coming decade  if the boom is truly just beginning as  with anything involving money be careful  do your research and know why you're  investing there are great communities on  reddit dedicated to different coins and  crypto as a whole so make sure you drop  in and learn from the pros if you do  decide to invest let me know your top  picks in the comments below who knows  maybe we'll all pick the right coin that  turns out to be bitcoin 2.0 if you  enjoyed this video consider subscribing  to support the channel and click the  little bell to be notified every time I  release a new video you can watch my  previous video by clicking here  or if you're really bored you can binge  